{"task": {"id": "I_kwDOUH0sFs8AAAABQaA7Cw", "item_id": "PVTI_lAHOAHSLSM4BlSCSzg978KI", "project_id": "PVT_kwHOAHSLSM4BlSCS", "number": 31, "title": "Map stored runtime and interaction evidence to Visparse analysis contracts", "body": "## Problem

Refloom can already invoke Visparse for a stored PNG/JPEG Asset and persist a Visparse Design Profile, but Refloom also captures runtime and interactive evidence that is not yet mapped into Visparse's runtime/interaction analysis contracts.

As a result, Refloom → Visparse integration currently supports static image design analysis but cannot yet make grounded use of stored runtime/interaction evidence for UX or interactive-experience analysis.

The mapping must be explicit. Passive captured Moments alone must not be treated as an action/transition sequence, and unavailable DOM/CSS/accessibility/Three.js signals must not be inferred or fabricated.

## Expected outcome

Allow Refloom to pass the runtime and interaction evidence it actually preserves into the appropriate Visparse analysis contracts, using the durable analysis lifecycle introduced by #30.

The implementation should first inspect the current Refloom capture/provenance data and current Visparse inspection/interaction contracts, then define and document the evidence mapping that is genuinely supported.

For supported evidence:

- bind Visparse inputs to the exact stored Refloom evidence and scope;
- preserve source identity and provenance;
- validate results with the real applicable Visparse contracts;
- reuse #30's durable analysis storage/lifecycle rather than creating a parallel analysis system;
- make the resulting analysis available through bounded UI/MCP retrieval as appropriate;
- preserve Visparse distinctions between measured/observed/inferred information and unknown/unavailable signals.

For unsupported or missing evidence, return an explicit unsupported/no-evidence outcome rather than guessing.

Capture authorization and analysis authorization should remain separate. This work should not implicitly add new browser actions, autonomous interaction, or duplicate Visparse analyzer logic inside Refloom.

If the desired Visparse contract requires evidence that Refloom does not currently capture, identify that gap explicitly. Add new capture capability only when it is necessary for the supported outcome and appropriately scoped; otherwise track it separately.

## Context

This is a follow-up to #30, which established the first durable Refloom → Visparse path for a single stored PNG/JPEG Asset → Design Profile.

Relevant Visparse capabilities include supplied runtime inspection evidence and explicit interaction-sequence analysis, but those contracts have different evidence requirements. A sequence of passive screenshots is not equivalent to recorded user actions and state transitions.

The implementation should avoid assuming:

- DOM/CSS/accessibility evidence exists when only screenshots were captured;
- Three.js scene information exists merely because a page uses WebGL;
- passive Moments encode an action sequence;
- one analysis contract can stand in for all runtime/UX analysis;
- cross-project Reference ownership or universal AI-provider support.

The goal is a small, truthful bridge between evidence Refloom really has and analysis Visparse can actually perform—not a general-purpose interaction platform or speculative capture framework.", "url": "https://github.com/takahirox/refloom/issues/31", "created_at": "2026-09-09T06:43:27Z", "state": "OPEN", "repository": "takahirox/refloom", "labels": ["task"], "priority": null, "status": "In Progress", "is_archived": false}, "context": {}, "resources": {}, "allocation": {}, "instruction": null, "run_id": "2f5c0c3565d945fb81b61b5eb924cdeb"}

